"""Sales tax. An order's subtotal is Rs 7,200 and sales tax is 18%.
 Print the tax amount and the total with tax (expected: 1296.0 and
  8496.0). Print the type of the tax amount. Why is it a float when
   the subtotal was an int?"""

   
subtotal = 7200
tax_rate = 18 / 100

tax_amount = subtotal * tax_rate
total = subtotal + tax_amount

print(tax_amount)
print(total)
print(type(tax_amount))
